e":"財報","count":5},{"name":"資料中心","count":2},{"name":"訂單/合約","count":2}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-11-04","period":"2026-09-27","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/804328/000080432826000128/qcom-20260927.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"We incorporated in California in 1985 and reincorporated in Delaware in 1991. We operate and report using a 52-53 week fiscal year ending on the last Sunday in September. Our 52-week fiscal years consist of four equal fiscal quarters of 13 weeks each, and our 53-week fiscal years consist of three 13-week fiscal quarters and one 14-week fiscal quarter. The financial results for our 53-week fiscal years and our 14-week fiscal quarters will not be exactly comparable to our 52-week fiscal years and our 13-week fiscal quarters. Our fiscal years for 2026, 2025 and 2024 included 52 weeks, 52 weeks and 53 weeks, respectively. Our fiscal year for 2027 will include 52 weeks.","zh":null},{"en":"We are a global technology leader, helping to bring intelligent computing everywhere through the development and commercialization of foundational technologies, including advanced artificial intelligence (AI), high-performance and low-power computing and leading connectivity. Our platforms help power intelligent products and services used around the world, across industries and applications from handsets to automotive, the internet of things (IoT) and data center.","zh":null},{"en":"In handsets, our Snapdragon platforms combine on-device AI, advanced wireless connectivity, high-performance and low-power computing and multimedia and imaging technologies to deliver differentiated smartphone experiences across a broad range of device tiers. In automotive, our Snapdragon Digital Chassis platforms, including connectivity, digital cockpit and advanced driver assistance and automated driving (ADAS/AD), are helping to connect the car to its environment and the cloud, creating unique in-cabin experiences and enabling a comprehensive assisted and automated driving solution. In IoT, our Snapdragon and Dragonwing platforms are helping power technology advancements in industries and applications from personal AI and compute (including personal computers (PCs), extended reality (XR) and other personal computing devices) to industrial, networking and robotics applications (includi","zh":null}],"markets":[],"customers":[],"competition":[],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2026-09-27","items":[{"name":"Qct","val":37208000000,"zh":"Qct"},{"name":"Qtl","val":5556000000,"zh":"Qtl"}],"total":43120000000}},"peers":["MU","AVGO","CSCO","AMD","ORCL"]}}